  "task_book": "docs/v0.1/M12F Coding.md §10 (损坏台账和持久化失败的 fail-closed 证据), §6, §4.1, §9",
  "what_this_table_is": "the refusals themselves: which damage a file was given, the word production answered with, whether it answered at the open or at an append, and the counts that show nothing happened afterwards — no calls, no sends, no repaired bytes. Each `refused_at` is the boundary the case actually crossed.",
  "what_this_table_is_not": "not a repair log. §6 forbids auto-repair, so no row here says a damaged ledger was fixed, and a row with `refused_at` = `append` describes a handle that was already open when the damage appeared — it is not a second way to pass the open gate. The two shapes are cross-checked apart, which is why `opened` appears only on the open rows."
